  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID-Wildlife Security</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;The purpose of this project is to protect endangered species in Uganda and eastern Democratic Republic of Congo from illegal wildlife trafficking. The project is intended to conserve great apes, elephants and other species by addressing the illegal hunting of great apes for meat, body parts and live infant pets and the slaughter of elephants for ivory through increasing the level of wildlife law enforcement and deterring potential traffickers from conducting these illegal activities. Specific activities include: 1) replication of the Last Great Ape Organization (LAGA) model for non-governmental organization (NGO) - government collaboration on wildlife law enforcement in Uganda and DRC, 2) setting a precedence of wildlife prosecution with a major wildlife criminal on trial in each country, 3) establishing sustainable national projects of wildlife law enforcement with a one arrest per week enforcement rate and creating a block of countries with functioning enforcement, and 4) establishing a model for sub-regional wildlife law enforcement using the model of investigations, arrest operations, legal assistance, media promotion and reporting. .&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
